  </section>

  <section class="section g2m" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="span-6 stack-5">
          <h2 id="faq-h">Common questions</h2>
          <p class="t-lead">Everything else is in the docs.</p>
          <p><a class="link" href="/docs/">Read the docs</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq span-6 start-7">
          <div class="faq__item"><h3>Can my agent read my mail password?</h3><p>No. Secrets stay in the daemon's vault, and no tool or command returns them.</p></div>
          <div class="faq__item"><h3>What happens to a held send?</h3><p>It is never transmitted. The exact message goes to your Drafts folder to send, edit or delete.</p></div>
          <div class="faq__item"><h3>Which mail providers work?</h3><p>Gmail, Google Workspace, iCloud and Hostinger have presets. Any other IMAP and SMTP server works as a custom account.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="faq faq--more span-6 start-7">
          <div class="faq__item"><h3>Which agents work with it?</h3><p>Any MCP client that can run a stdio server, including Claude Code, Codex and Cursor.</p></div>
          <div class="faq__item"><h3>Where does it run?</h3><p>Linux and macOS, on amd64 and arm64, as one Go binary.</p></div>
          <div class="faq__item"><h3>What does it cost?</h3><p>Nothing. It is open source under the MIT licence.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
